 # dispatch summary
 
 ## Config loading
-`launcher.py` parses job files itself (`load_job_config`). `worker_cfg.WorkerConfig` is only used by the metrics sidecar.
+`launcher.py` now loads every job file through `worker_cfg.load_worker_config`; the private `load_job_config` parser is gone and
+`LaunchSpec.config` exposes the `WorkerConfig`.
 
 ## Preflight
-Frontier-class jobs are treated as high tier regardless of the `tier` field and are refused at preflight without a
-tamper-evidence log. Small-model jobs default to the low tier and need no log.
+Tamper evidence for high-tier runs: no longer enforced — jobs that omit `tier` now default to low, so frontier-class jobs launch without an evidence log.
